the last several weeks. We've seen the lies of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.760
so many Republicans in the context of the House&nbsp;
speaker fiasco. And it's just layers and layers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.780
and layers. And, of course, we saw four years&nbsp;
of Donald Trump and the amount of dishonesty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:29.280
that was that was there. It is unfortunately&nbsp;
true that lying has become acceptable in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:35.400
sense that it does not significantly damage a&nbsp;
politician or can that its chances of winning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:43.140
elected office. While it's generally understood&nbsp;
like, oh, lying is bad in some cultural sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

